# Platform — portal registration intake (multi-workspace)

**Status:** 2026-06-30 · Track A registry in `@app-tour/workspace-sdk`

**Related:** [platform-portal-registration.mdoc](../phase-17/platform-portal-registration.mdoc) · [public-catalog.md](../workspaces/denali/public-catalog.md) § Adding a workspace

---

## Layering (frozen)

```text
apps/portal (shell)
  OTP · profile · intake UI slots
  BFF POST /api/catalog/registrations
       │
       ▼
@app-tour/workspace-sdk (registry + contracts)
  resolveCatalogRegistrationApiPath(pluginId)
  resolveCatalogIntakeCapabilities(pluginId)
  buildCatalogRegistrationUpstreamRequest(pluginId, payload)
  PublicCatalogTransportSnapshot + transport intake helpers
  RegistrationIntakeRecord (persisted booking JSON)
       │
       ▼
packages/workspaces/{id} (business rules)
  HTTP POST /{id}/registrations
  validate payload · duplicate guards · normalize transport
  map canonical → PublicCatalogCard egress fields
       │
       ▼
apps/api (host adapters)
  BookingsRepository.registrationIntake JSONB
  identity/me profile fields
```

**Rule:** `apps/portal` and `apps/marketing` **must not** `static-import` `@app-tour/workspace-{id}`. They only use **SDK registries** + catalog card shape from HTTP.

**Rule:** Workspace-specific duplicate logic, transport normalization, and Zod schemas live under `packages/workspaces/{id}/`. SDK owns **cross-workspace contracts** and **portal dispatch**.

---

## SDK registry (Track A)

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `supportsCatalogRegistration(pluginId)` | Marketing/register CTA gate — manifest **L2+** (`WORKSPACE_GUEST_CONFORMANCE_LEVELS`); marketing shell does not bootstrap intake plugin registry |
| `resolveCatalogRegistrationApiPath(pluginId)` | `POST /denali/registrations` · `/urban/registrations` |
| `resolveCatalogIntakeCapabilities(pluginId)` | Portal UI modules (tabs, transport, email, idempotency) |
| `buildCatalogRegistrationUpstreamRequest(pluginId, payload)` | BFF body + path + extra headers |
| `resolvePublicCatalogTransportIntake(...)` | Transport UI visibility (card-driven, no workspace import) |
| `computePublicCatalogRegistrationPricePerPerson(...)` | Portal price hint only |
| `parseRegistrationIntakeRecord(raw)` | Operator display / transport roster |

Adding workspace `{id}`:

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | Add paths to `resolve-catalog-registration-api-path.ts` |
| 2 | Add capabilities + request profile to `resolve-catalog-intake-capabilities.ts` |
| 3 | Extend `build-catalog-registration-upstream-request.ts` if new POST shape |
| 4 | Implement `POST /{id}/registrations` in workspace HTTP |
| 5 | Extend `publicCatalog.toCatalogCard` if new egress fields drive intake |
| 6 | Document workspace deltas in `docs/workspaces/{id}/` (not in portal shell doc) |

---

## Request profiles (v1)

| Profile | Plugins | POST shape |
|---------|---------|------------|
| `denali_contact_v1` | denali | `{ tourId, registrantTarget?, contact{...}, partySize, transport? }` |
| `urban_email_v1` | urban | `{ tourId, contact{ email, fullName, phone? }, partySize, notes? }` + `Idempotency-Key` |

Portal BFF **never** branches on `pluginId === "denali"` inline — it calls `buildCatalogRegistrationUpstreamRequest`.

---

## Intake capabilities matrix

| Capability | Denali | Urban | Default (unknown) |
|------------|--------|-------|-------------------|
| `registrantTargetTabs` | yes | no | no |
| `transportIntake` | yes (when card has `transport`) | no | no |
| `participantProfileFields` | nationalId, fatherName, birthDate | — | — |
| `emailAtIntake` | no (profile only) | yes | no |
| `notesAtIntake` | no | yes | no |
| `idempotencyKey` | no | yes | no |
| `successDataAttributes` | — | `data-urban-registration-success` | — |

Transport UI is **card-driven**: when `PublicCatalogCard.transport` is absent, portal shows no transport controls even if `transportIntake` capability is true.

### Denali tour-flag intake gating (2026-07-02)

`IntakeSchemaContext.tourRequirements` carries catalog egress flags (`nationalIdRequired`, `fatherNameRequired`, `birthDateRequired`). Denali `resolveEffectiveSchema` applies:

1. **Tour filter** — omit participant fields when the matching canonical flag is not `true`.
2. **Session filter** — for `registrantTarget=self`, omit fields already present on `GET /api/me/profile`.

`RegistrationFlowContext.tourRequirements` is populated from catalog detail HTTP (`fetchCatalogTour` in portal). Workspace intake plugins own filter logic; portal shell only passes flags.

Smoke fixture tours (operator tenant `…000014`):

| Tour ID | Title | Purpose |
|---------|-------|---------|
| `…000210` | North Ridge Trek | Default registration smoke (SMK-PTL-01) — no participant flags, no transport |
| `…000211` | Denali draft fixture | Draft 404 probes |
| `…000212` | Alpine Identity Check | DEN-INTAKE / DEN-PROF — `nationalIdRequired` + `fatherNameRequired` + `birthDateRequired` |
| `…000213` | Ridge Bus Shuttle | DEN-TRANS-01/02 — `transport.mode=bus` · `allowPersonalCar=true` · `transportCost` (organized default + personal-car opt-in) |
| `…000214` | Carpool Pass | DEN-TRANS-03 — `transport.mode=shared_cars` · `dongAmount` (mandatory transport follow-up) |

API catalog list returns **four** published tours (`210` + `212` + `213` + `214`) when `ensureOperatorSmokeSeedTour()` runs. Tours `213`/`214` carry canonical `transport.*` so the portal renders transport intake without any workspace import (card-driven via `PublicCatalogCard.transport`).

When `emailAtIntake` is true and member profile has no saved email, portal intake shows an email field (Urban). Profile-step email still pre-fills when present.

When `notesAtIntake` is true, portal shows optional notes textarea (Urban).

---

## Persisted booking metadata

`BookingsRepository.registrationIntake` JSON (egress-safe, ops-only):

```json
{
  "registrantTarget": "self",
  "transport": { "kind": "primary" },
  "nationalId": "1234567890"
}
```

Parsed via SDK `RegistrationIntakeRecord` — operator web imports SDK parser, not workspace packages.

Workspace-specific validation of `transport.kind` remains in `packages/workspaces/denali/` Zod schemas aligned with SDK enum.

